{
  "name": "Autoscaler Lags a Black Friday Ramp",
  "description": "Black Friday 00:00 UTC. Promo emails fire and traffic ramps from 200 rps to 4500 rps in under five minutes. The HPA's 60-second scale window plus the 90-second pod warm-up means the existing replicas eat the spike — p95 latency hits the SLA cliff.",
  "reasoning": "An nginx ingress, four Go API replicas, and a Postgres + Redis. As traffic ramps, the four existing replicas saturate; the autoscaler eventually adds capacity but with a visible delay.",
